A||N||7||Xenon||I'm looking for data on connects to dashboard for a custom digital solution.||||5||
Z||000000||Xenon||05-25-2001||01:18 AM||||While installing a remote car starter/alarm setup, I noticed that the Fieros has the perfect dashboard setup for doing a custom digital replacement since it has no mechanical moving parts going to the dash such as the speedometer cable on most cars. I have a 1986 SE V6 and I am trying to see if any one knows the specs for the plugs that plug directly into the dash/gauge set. The indicators are simple enough to figure out with a multimeter, but I am trying to find info on the connections that control the 4 analog gauges (speed, tach, gas, temp). Any help would be great!!! Thanks.<BR>~Shawn||||reg||5
Z||000001||Xenon||05-25-2001||12:08 PM||||The manual has a lot of the wire color coding and locations. As well as schematics of most of the basic wiring. But some things seem incorrect. The manual says that the speedometer sending unit is 1-wire YELLOW and 1-wire PURPLE. With a BLK/WHT ground wire and a BROWN wire output to the fuel injection system. But a 5-wire connector goes to the speedometer and I have the BROWN wire and the BLK/WHT ground wire, but the purple wire there is PURPLE/WHT and the I have a YELLOW and the last wire is YELLOW/BLK.<BR>   Anyways, the manual is not perfectly written for my 1986 SE V6; it's just the Haynes manual. So I need help on finding the exact wire codes to the Speed/Tach/Gas/Temp gauages. Thanks.<BR>~Shawn||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||05-25-2001||12:53 PM||||Welcome to the forum....<BR>Check this site out, it has the Fiero diagrams posted.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm</A> <BR>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 GT Fastback Ratmatic<BR>Red 84 4 speed<p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 05-25-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||DecadenceR||05-25-2001||01:17 PM||||In my site searches, I have found a few places that make replacement digital dashes for Fieros. <A HREF="http://www.pennock.nl/fdd-x1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pennock.nl/fdd-x1.htm</A> <BR>This is one. I have to find the other link.... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Xenon||05-25-2001||01:36 PM||||   Eric_PA,   that's an awesome link to diagrams and wiring info!!!! Looks like it will have all the info I need.<P>   As for the digital dashboards available as aftermarket units; there are some extremely nice units out there. But the cost is so very HIGH. And since I enjoy doing anything electronic within my means, I believe I can make my own custom digital dash board replacement for much cheaper and completely custom. $800-3500 for a complete gauge replacement only is way too expensive for just gauges for me. Also I plan on have a computer interface to control a TFT color laptop screen in the future. My main goal is to extremely reduce the gauge pod size to make the interior feel more roomy and look more updated.<P> Thanks a ton for that link to the wiring info!!! Awesome info!!! Now if I can only get a rotary engine conversion kit! Thanks again.<BR>~Shawn||||reg||7
Z||000005||Cliff D.||05-25-2001||10:46 PM||||That project sounds cool man. I know zip about electronics and less about computers, but I have this vision of someday designing a filter set similar to a graphic equalizer to dictate values to the ecm. This was my answer to the scca "improved touring" rule book which says you can't mess with the ecm, but you can use resistors and all to change sensor values. Anyway, it looks like they are going to allow alternate chips in 2002 so my crazy project may never happen....unless I finally decide to learn something. Good luck, I'd be interested in one of your prototypes if you succeed.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Xenon||05-25-2001||11:10 PM||||Here is the exact dashboard wiring I was looking for. Sent to me in an email. Is it possible to attach files to a post? "copy-paste" doesn't seem to look so hot here.<P>Fiero - wiring to dashboard<P>C204 Speedometer (5-wires) 18-pin connector (BOTTOM)<BR>----------------------------------------------------<BR>P   Black/White  = Ground<BR>R   Purple/White = from Speed Sensor (pin A)<BR>S   Yellow       = from Speed Sensor (pin B)<BR>T   Yellow/Black = 12V + from 'Radio' Fuse (10AMP)<BR>U   Brown        = VSS signal - OUTPUT to electronic fuel injection system<P><BR>C205 Gauges and Indicators 12-pin connector (LEFT side)<BR>-------------------------------------------------------<BR>04  Black        = Ground for Coolant Temp Gauge (from G201)<BR>07  Grey         = Illumination<BR>09  Pink/Black   = 12V + from 'Gauge' fuse (10AMP)<BR>10  Dark Green   = Hood/Trunk/Door Ajar indicator lamp<BR>11  Light Green  = Coolant Temp sender to Temp Gauge  *** NOTE 1<BR>12  Grey         = Illumination<P><BR>C206 Gauges and Indicators 18-pin connector (RIGHT side)<BR>--------------------------------------------------------<BR>01  Tan/Black       = Upshift Indicator (from MPFI)<BR>02  Lt Blue(2wires) = Left-hand Turn Indicator<BR>03  Grey            = Illumination<BR>04  Dk Blue(2wires) = Right-hand Turn Indicator<BR>05  Pink/Black      = Charge Indicator (from 'Gauge' fuse (10AMP))<BR>06  Brown           = Charge Indicator (from charging system)<BR>07  Pink            = to Fuel Gauge   *** NOTE 3<BR>08  Yellow          = Fasten Seat Beat Indicator<BR>09  Pink/Black      = 12V + from 'Gauge' fuse (10AMP)<BR>10  Brown/black     = Check Engine light (from MPFI)<BR>11  Black           = Ground (from G201)<BR>12  Light Green     = Hi Beam Indicator<BR>13  Dark Green      = Coolant Temp Warning Indicator   *** NOTE 2<BR>14  Tan/White       = Brake Warning Indicator<BR>15  Grey            = Illumination<BR>16  --------------- = Unused<BR>17  Tan             = Oil Pressure Warning Indicator   *** NOTE 4<BR>18  White           = Tachometer (From MPFI)<P>NOTES:<BR>1   Sender resistance: 1365ohms @ 100F (38C), 55ohms at 260F (127C).<BR>2   Switch to ground: closed above 257F (125C), open below 230F (110C).<BR>3   Sender resistance: 90ohms at full, Zero ohms at empty.<BR>4   Switch to Ground: Open above 4 psi.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000007||Xenon||05-25-2001||11:13 PM||||Actually, "copy-paste" worked pretty well. Attaching files would still be cool. I can't wait to get some interface circuits setup to completely handle the entire dash components and the oil pressure/voltmeter pod! The Fiero also has the perfect tail lens assemblies for modifing!||||reg||7
